Electrical Apparatus Service Association and Association of Electrical and Mechanical Trades. The Effect of Repair/Rewinding on Premium Efficiency/IE3 Motors, full report, version 0121, copyright 2021. [Complete 38-file-page report](https://www.theaemt.com/static/831edc09-78f0-4ae5-a9e33fafa5a7bc69/Reference-The-Rewind-Study-Full-Report.pdf) · [Publisher study page](https://www.theaemt.com/resource/the-effect-of-repair-rewinding-on-premium-ie3-motor-efficiency.html) · [Separate Good Practice Guide](https://easa.com/ansi/good-practice-guide-to-maintain-motor-efficiency).

Read both complete studies in the report, including methods, losses, error sources, test data and limitations. Compare repair/rewind variables with actual efficiency and condition evidence. Read the separate full good-practice guide through its authorized publisher route for repair methods; do not mistake the report for that current independent guide.

Title, version, contents and copyright were inspected on 29 October 2026. The 2019 study is supplied in a 2021 file that also includes the 2003 report; later website posting dates are distinct. Study results apply to the tested motors/methods, not every possible repair. Free report access does not supply a blanket open-adaptation licence or every training resource. No report, guide or data is copied here.

